# Participant buckets (office language)

Use **only** these five labels when talking to Victor or labelling office UI about families / kids. Do **not** say “former”, “formal”, “alumni”, “ex-client”, or “interested” unless mapping to these.

| Label | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| **CLIENT** | On services now — has Autumn 2026/27 (or current term) slots / standing seats. Appear in Sessions, LOCAL board, MADRE as named participants. |
| **REGISTERED** | Completed the **registration form**, but have **never** been clients (never had a paid/confirmed service seat with us). |
| **LEADS** | Enquired and got **OTP**, but did **not** finish registration. |
| **OLD** | Were clients (had services with us) but **from September 2026** they have **no slots**. Not in Sessions as booked kids. |
| **WAITING** | Registered and want a service that is **full** — on the wait / waiting list for a place. |

## Mapping (code / old wording → bucket)

- `active_client` / on roster / in services → **CLIENT**
- `registered` / registration submitted, never seated → **REGISTERED**
- OTP started, registration incomplete → **LEADS**
- Aug15 unpaid release / no Sep+ seats (e.g. Karo, Kareena, Shire) → **OLD** (not “former”)
- Waitlist / full service queue → **WAITING**

## Sessions / standing

- **CLIENT** only on Autumn Sessions roster and LOCAL named seats.
- **OLD** / **REGISTERED** / **LEADS** / **WAITING** must not appear as booked Sessions feedback units (open seats = No participant).
- Rule companion: `.cursor/rules/former-clients-not-in-sessions.mdc` (those three are **OLD**).

## Admin UI labels (nav / pages)

| Bucket | Admin surface |
|--------|----------------|
| **CLIENT** | Nav + page formerly “Participants” (`clients`) |
| **REGISTERED** | Nav + page formerly “Registration forms” (`portal_participant_documents`) |
| **LEADS** | Nav + page formerly “Enquiries & intake” (`leads`) |
| **WAITING** | Nav + page formerly “Waiting list” (`c4k_waitlist`) |
| **OLD** | Filter / pill on CLIENT list (`old_participants`) — not a separate nav tab |

A person can move buckets over time (e.g. LEADS → REGISTERED → WAITING → CLIENT, or CLIENT → OLD).
